From: OpenWrt developers <openwrt@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: keep software flooding with wireless bridge ports

The VLAN-unaware PPE bridge TX flooding optimization submits one broadcast
copy and asks EDMA to replicate it using a physical-port bitmap. Wireless
VAPs in br-lan remain software bridge ports and are not represented in that
bitmap. With a VAP present, the optimization can therefore consume a DHCP
broadcast without delivering a copy to the physical uplink.

Keep the PPE bridge and unicast offload, but use the normal software bridge
flooding path for VLAN-unaware bridges so broadcasts and unknown multicasts
are cloned to every software and hardware port correctly.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt developers <openwrt@example.invalid>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_bridge.c
@@ -890,7 +890,7 @@ static int ppe_bridge_port_join(struct ppe_bridge *pb,
 	ret = switchdev_bridge_port_offload(dev, dev, pb,
 					    &pb->switchdev_nb,
 					    &pb->switchdev_blocking_nb,
-					    !vlan_aware, extack);
+					    false, extack);
 	if (ret)
 		goto err_offload;
-- 
